pedal-companions — third-party material
=======================================

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the code and the original work here: the
HTML, CSS and JavaScript, the SVG drawings of the pedals, the layout and the
interaction design.

It does not cover the material below, which belongs to the manufacturers named
and is not ours to sublicense. The MIT grant should not be read as doing so.


Descriptions taken from the manuals
-----------------------------------

Each companion quotes its maker's own manual rather than paraphrasing it, so
the writing describing what a control does is largely theirs:

  Chase Bliss Audio — Lost + Found. The twenty-four mode descriptions, the
  per-mode tips, the knob descriptions and the descriptions of the sixteen dip
  switches, quoted or closely adapted from the Lost + Found manual. Roughly
  1,700 words.

  Strymon — Volante. The knob and switch descriptions and the notes on the
  machine types, quoted from the Volante user manual, Rev E. A few hundred
  words.

  Fulltone — OCD-Germanium. The control descriptions and the notes on power
  and gain, quoted from the CS-OCD-Ge manual. A few hundred words.

  JHS — Muffuletta. The six circuit descriptions and the knob descriptions,
  quoted or closely adapted from what JHS publish for the Muffuletta at
  jhspedals.info. A few hundred words.

  JHS — PackRat. The nine circuit histories and descriptions and the knob
  descriptions, quoted or closely adapted from what JHS publish for the
  PackRat at jhspedals.info. Roughly 500 words.

Copyright in that text remains with the manufacturer it came from.

The rest — the drawings of the enclosures, the mode-picker, the printed-page
indexes, the glosses on the makers' terms of art, and the notes marked as
inferred rather than documented — was written for this site and is covered by
the MIT licence.


Product photography
-------------------

The index page carries one product photograph per pedal, taken from each
manufacturer's own site and processed for this index — background removed,
trimmed and centred on a common canvas. The processing is ours; the
photographs are not. Copyright in each remains with the manufacturer that
published it.


